    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Merge Intervals\n\nGiven an array of intervals where intervals[i] = [start_i, end_i], merge all overlapping intervals and return an array of the non-overlapping intervals that cover all the intervals in the input.\n\nExample: [[1,3],[2,6],[8,10],[15,18]] -> [[1,6],[8,10],[15,18]].\nConstraints: 1 <= len(intervals) <= 10^4.",
      "id": "m-1",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-09T23:18:59.749Z",
      "durationMs": 0
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "channel": "analysis",
      "content": "Constraints are small enough that the obvious approach fits, but the follow-up asks for the optimal one; going straight to it.\n\nEdge cases to cover before submitting: empty input, single element, and the all-duplicates case.\n\nComplexity check: one pass, O(n) time, O(n) auxiliary space for the map. That meets the constraint.\n\nWriting the solution, then tracing it on the first example to confirm indices are handled correctly.",
      "id": "m-2",
      "timestamp": "2026-03-09T23:19:00.036Z",
      "durationMs": 6328,
      "stepIndex": 1
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "channel": "commentary",
      "content": "",
      "toolCalls": [
        {
          "id": "call-1",
          "name": "execute_code",
          "arguments": "{\"language\":\"python3\",\"code\":\"class Solution:\\n    def merge(self, intervals: list[list[int]]) -> list[list[int]]:\\n        intervals.sort()\\n        out = [intervals[0][:]]\\n        for s, e in intervals[1:]:\\n            if s < out[-1][1]:\\n                out[-1][1] = max(out[-1][1], e)\\n            else:\\n                out.append([s, e])\\n        return out\"}",
          "parsedArguments": {
            "language": "python3",
            "code": "class Solution:\n    def merge(self, intervals: list[list[int]]) -> list[list[int]]:\n        intervals.sort()\n        out = [intervals[0][:]]\n        for s, e in intervals[1:]:\n            if s < out[-1][1]:\n                out[-1][1] = max(out[-1][1], e)\n            else:\n                out.append([s, e])\n        return out"
          }
        }
      ],
